## Local development

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `make dev` | Full stack via `docker-compose.yml` + `docker-compose.dev.yml` (Postgres 18, API hot-reload, Web, gateway) |
| `make down` | Stop compose stack |
| `make api` | Run Quarkus dev locally (outside Docker) |
| `make web` | Run Next.js dev locally |
| `make test` | Maven tests |
| `make postgres-volume-reset` | Reset Postgres volume after major PG upgrades |

API dev in Docker uses `Dockerfile.dev` + `gosu` entrypoint running `./mvnw quarkus:dev`.

---
## Testing

- Framework: Quarkus JUnit + REST Assured.
- Location: `apps/api/quarkus/src/test/java/`.
- Naming: `{Entity}ResourceTest.java` for HTTP behavior; `*IT.java` for integration when needed.
- Module unit tests: `./mvnw -pl modules/{entity} test`.
- Prefer status codes, response shape, and key field behavior over mocking repositories.
- Tests may require Docker/Postgres; `%test` profile disables Flyway/Hibernate when configured for unit-only runs.

After API changes:

```bash
./mvnw -pl apps/api/quarkus -am test
# compile-only fallback when DB unavailable:
./mvnw -pl apps/api/quarkus -am -DskipTests compile
```

