## Verification checklist (new entity)

```
- [ ] Flyway in migrations/ AND db/migration/
- [ ] EntityTypes constant
- [ ] modules/{entity} domain + tests
- [ ] EntityRecord join + {Entity}Record + repositories
- [ ] {Entity}Service (two-table create, version check, audit events)
- [ ] {Entity}Resource + DTOs + validation mapper
- [ ] SeasonResourceTest-style HTTP tests
- [ ] Next.js lib + UI (see nextjs-frontend.mdc)
```

For the full end-to-end workflow, use the **create-plm-entity** skill.

---
## Do not

- Skip the dual Flyway migration copy.
- Put business validation in REST resources or JPA entity callbacks.
- Hard-delete kernel rows — archive via terminal status on `EntityRecord`.
- Call `UUID.randomUUID()` for entity IDs — rely on `@UuidGenerator(VERSION_7)` on flush.
- Add Spring, javax.persistence, or `@Transactional` from Spring.
- Create a new exception mapper per status code — reuse `NotFoundExceptionMapper`, `ConflictExceptionMapper`, `{Entity}ValidationExceptionMapper`.
- Enable Hibernate schema generation or drift from Flyway-managed DDL.
- Add auth/Cerbos enforcement unless explicitly requested.